{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/11643","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/11643/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/11643/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/11643/events","html_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/11643","id":645862501,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWU2NDU4NjI1MDE=","number":11643,"title":"bazel-3.3.0 fails to bootstrap on ppc64le","user":{"login":"ceseo","id":7077164,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzcxNjQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7077164?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ceseo","html_url":"https://github.com/ceseo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ceseo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ceseo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ceseo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ceseo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ceseo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ceseo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ceseo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ceseo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ceseo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":106503259,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMDY1MDMyNTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/labels/type:%20bug","name":"type: bug","color":"0052cc","default":false,"description":null},{"id":1020665933,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMDIwNjY1OTMz","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/labels/untriaged","name":"untriaged","color":"c34ddd","default":false,"description":""},{"id":1459044053,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNDU5MDQ0MDUz","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/labels/team-OSS","name":"team-OSS","color":"f1f442","default":false,"description":"Issues for the Bazel OSS team: installation, release processBazel packaging, website"}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2020-06-25T21:29:26Z","updated_at":"2020-07-02T09:46:07Z","closed_at":"2020-07-02T09:46:07Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"\r\n\r\n### Description of the problem / feature request:\r\n\r\nWhile bootstrapping bazel-3.3.0 on ppc64le:\r\n\r\n```\r\nIn file included from src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/syntax/cpu_profiler_posix.cc:20:0:\r\nbazel-out/ppc-opt/bin/external/bazel_tools/tools/jdk/include/jni.h:45:10: fatal error: jni_md.h: No such file or directory\r\n #include \"jni_md.h\"\r\n          ^~~~~~~~~~\r\ncompilation terminated.\r\nTarget //src:bazel_nojdk failed to build\r\nINFO: Elapsed time: 173.915s, Critical Path: 19.09s\r\nINFO: 735 processes: 735 local.\r\nFAILED: Build did NOT complete successfully\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis is probably because `jni_md.h` is in `jdk/include/linux`, not `jdk/include`. Looking at the JDK installation path on Ubuntu 18.04:\r\n```\r\nubuntu@horus:~$ sudo find / -name jni_md.h\r\n/usr/lib/jvm/java-8-openjdk-ppc64el/include/linux/jni_md.h\r\n/usr/lib/jvm/java-11-openjdk-ppc64el/include/linux/jni_md.h\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Bugs: what's the simplest, easiest way to reproduce this bug? Please provide a minimal example if possible.\r\n\r\nJust try a bootstrap build on ppc64le.\r\n\r\n### What operating system are you running Bazel on?\r\n\r\nUbuntu 18.04.3\r\n\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"bazel-io","id":15028808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/b